From c2e8fefdd797560c9ede1c64d807d00d6cf91ba2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:03:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] S2-9: workshop panels shown last, unit tests for the new
 ui helpers, floors, docs

The workshop's kept panels are shown after everything else in the frame (a
panel shown earlier makes every later 2D call over its box take the GBA's
slow checked path: the stat bars cost 9.7 ms instead of ~4). The part list's
rect starts below row 0's cursor pill and ends above the last row's, the
hole is the 12-row pill (a panel hole must hold the whole box of every 2D
call drawn over it), and with the cursor on row 1 or the second to last row
the list is drawn whole. test_panel: ui_window_open, ui_bar_still,
ui_backdrop_flat and ui_style_use each against what they replace; the
workshop's lost-panel redraw is compared pixel for pixel with the kept one.
The Dreamcast build keeps no panels (WS_KEPT 0: unused parameter fixed).

expect-fps 28 floors on the three workshop windows of speed2_action.txt.
Docs: GBA.md "Speed wave 2: S2-9" with the RAM ledger row (EWRAM 1,788 ->
1,620 B free), PS1.md, DREAMCAST.md, ROADMAP.md. The two saved wip patches
of this package are deleted (their content is in the branch).

GBA (libmgba, speed2 action): workshop 18.7 -> 30.0 fps, part change 23.4
-> 30.0, armory 26.7 -> 30.0, every frame 2 vblanks. PS1 28.78 -> 30.12.
Dreamcast: no tick over 33.3 ms, worst 22.7 ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
